# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback for the client-only routes.
#
# `npm run build` prerenders one index.html per *indexable* route
# (scripts/prerender.mjs, driven by INDEXABLE_ROUTES in src/lib/seo.js),
# so /, /with-jd, /without-jd and /pricing each resolve to a real file on
# disk and need no rule here. The five routes below are marked `noindex`
# in src/lib/seo.js -- they are authenticated or render differently per
# user -- so they are deliberately not prerendered, have no file, and a
# direct hit or a refresh on one 404s without this.
#
# Listed explicitly rather than as a `/* /index.html 200` catch-all so a
# genuinely mistyped URL still returns a real 404, instead of a soft 404
# rendering an empty page with a 200. The cost is that a NEW client-only
# route must be added here -- and to the `rewrites` in ../../vercel.json,
# which mirrors this list -- or it will 404 on refresh in production
# while working perfectly under `npm run dev`.
#
# Vite copies public/ verbatim into the build output, so this file ships
# to frontend-react-dist/_redirects, which is where Cloudflare Pages
# looks for it.
/dashboard  /index.html  200
/settings   /index.html  200
/history    /index.html  200
/login      /index.html  200
/signup     /index.html  200
